Third-party and derived components
----------------------------------

1. python/fast_data/   — vendored from the FNO4d repository, path `loc_libs/fast_data`.
   See python/fast_data/UPSTREAM.json for the exact commit and per-file checksums.
   Author: Joern Putschke. Original work, with the exception noted below.

2. python/fast_data/liquefier/   — DERIVED WORK.
   This subpackage is a pure-Python port of X-SCAPE's causal liquefier:

       src/liquefier/CausalLiquefier.{h,cc}
       src/framework/LiquefierBase.{h,cc}

   X-SCAPE is distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later by The JETSCAPE Collaboration.
   The port therefore inherits that licence, and this contribution as a whole is
   released under GPL-3.0-or-later for that reason.

   Physics reference for the kernel:
       Y. Tachibana et al., causal (telegraph) diffusion of jet-deposited
       energy-momentum; see the X-SCAPE sources above.

3. The MC-Glauber (python/fast_data/glauber.py) is original code, not derived from
   MUSIC, superMC, iEBE or TRENTo. Its physics references are:
       Bozek & Wyskiel, tilted source          — arXiv:1002.4999
       Broniowski & Bozek, string fluctuations — arXiv:1509.04124
   Its only coupling to MUSIC is file-format compatibility with MUSIC's EoS tables.


Open licensing question
-----------------------
At the time of writing, the js-contrib repository has no top-level LICENSE file, and
neither does FNO4d. A GPLv3 derivative (item 2 above) living inside an unlicensed
repository is ambiguous. This should be resolved with the js-contrib maintainer before
this contribution is published.
